     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\">Hi,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\">It may be possible. The key issue is not with Canopy but with the fact that it might be hard to call somatic point mutations and CNAs without a normal control. These are used as input for Canopy and they are\r\n non-trivial. See the links below for more info on this.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\"><a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/Canopy/blob/master/instruction/SNA_CNA_input.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/Canopy/blob/master/instruction/SNA_CNA_input.md&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498465682000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0I6joAW-Zn4b--3anmhzBK\">https://github.com/yuchaojiang/Canopy/blob/master/instruction/SNA_CNA_input.md</a>\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\"><a href=\"https://github.com/yuchaojiang/Canopy/blob/master/instruction/SNA_CNA_choice.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yuchaojiang/Canopy/blob/master/instruction/SNA_CNA_choice.md&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792498465682000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1KCW25brNUTG98v4LEWH31\">https://github.com/yuchaojiang/Canopy/blob/master/instruction/SNA_CNA_choice.md</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\">Yuchao<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #e1e1e1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>From:</b> Sugganth Daniel [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sda...@foundationmedicine.com</a>]\r\n<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Friday, June 30, 2017 2:13 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">yuc...@mail.med.upenn.edu</a><br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> Canopy<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hello Yuchao,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I read your paper with a lot of interest. Is it possible to use Canopy on tumor targeted panel sequencing without a matched normal?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white\"><b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;color:#77933c\"><u></u> <u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white\">Thanks,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white\">Sugganth<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white\"><b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;color:#77933c\"><u></u> <u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white\"><b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;color:#77933c\"><u></u> <u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white\"><b><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;color:#77933c\">Sugganth Daniel, M.D.,\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:white\"><b><i><s